<SubSection title="Machining Types" id="Machining Types">
<Itemize>

    <Item><strong>Milling</strong>: Rotating tool removes material from stationary workpiece.</Item>
    <Item><strong>Turning</strong>: Stationary tool removes material from rotating workpiece.</Item>
    <Item><strong>Drilling</strong>: Rotating drill bit creates holes in the workpiece.</Item>

</Itemize>
</SubSection>
<SubSection title="Cutting Geometry" id="Cutting Geometry">
<p>image of cutting geometry (slide 16)</p>
<Itemize>

    <Item>Terms: Rake angle <InlineEquation equation="\\alpha" />, Shear angle <InlineEquation equation="\\phi" />, Chip thickness <InlineEquation equation="t_c" />, Depth of cut <InlineEquation equation="t_o" />, Length of shear plane <InlineEquation equation="l_s" /></Item>
    <Item>Chip ratio: <InlineEquation equation="r = \\frac{t_o}{t_c}" /></Item>
    <Item>Shear angle: <InlineEquation equation="\\tan \\phi = \\frac{r \\cos \\alpha}{1 - r \\sin \\alpha}" /></Item>

</Itemize>
</SubSection>
<SubSection title="Cutting Forces" id="Cutting Forces">
<p>image of cutting forces (slide 18/19)</p>
<p>Friction angle <InlineEquation equation="\\beta" />, Coefficient of friction <InlineEquation equation="\\mu = \\tan \\beta" />, Resultant <InlineEquation equation="R" /></p>
</SubSection>
<SubSubSection title="Tool-Chip Interface" id="Tool-Chip Interface">
<Itemize>

    <Item>Friction force <InlineEquation equation="F = R \\sin \\beta" /></Item>
    <Item>Normal Force <InlineEquation equation="N = R \\cos \\beta" /></Item>

</Itemize>
</SubSubSection>
<SubSubSection title="Vertical &amp Horizontal" id="Vertical &amp Horizontal">
<Itemize>

    <Item>Thrust force <InlineEquation equation="F_t = R \\sin(\\beta - \\alpha)" /></Item>
    <Item>Cutting force <InlineEquation equation="F_c = R \\cos(\\beta - \\alpha)" /></Item>

</Itemize>
</SubSubSection>
<SubSubSection title="Shear Plane" id="Shear Plane">
<Itemize>

    <Item>Normal force <InlineEquation equation="N_s = R \\sin(\\beta - \\alpha + \\phi)" />    </Item>
    <Item>Shear force <InlineEquation equation="F_s = R \\cos(\\beta - \\alpha + \\phi)" />    </Item>
    <Item>Shear Stress <InlineEquation equation="T = \\frac{F_s}{A_s} = \\frac{R \\cos(\\beta - \\alpha + \\phi) \\sin\\phi}{w t_0}" /></Item>

</Itemize>
<p>*box</p>
<p>To minimize the shear stress, differentiate with respect to the shear plane angle <InlineEquation equation="\\phi" /> and set the derivative equal to zero:</p>
<DisplayEquation
  equation="\\frac{d}{d\\phi}\\left(\\cos(\\beta - \\alpha + \\phi)\\sin\\phi\\right)"
  title=""
/>
</SubSubSection>

<SubSubSection
  title="Differentiation with Respect to phi"
  id="Differentiation-with-Respect-to-phi">

<DisplayEquation
  equation="0 = \\frac{d}{d\\phi}\\left(\\frac{R}{w t_o}\\cos(\\beta - \\alpha + \\phi)\\sin\\phi\\right)"
  title=""
/>

<DisplayEquation
  equation="\\frac{d}{d\\phi}\\left(\\cos(\\beta - \\alpha + \\phi)\\sin\\phi\\right)"
  title=""
/>

Applying the product rule:

<DisplayEquation
  equation="0 = \\cos(\\beta - \\alpha + \\phi)\\cos\\phi - \\sin(\\beta - \\alpha + \\phi)\\sin\\phi"
  title=""
/>

Rearranging terms:


<DisplayEquation
  equation="\\sin(\\beta - \\alpha + \\phi)\\sin\\phi   = \\cos(\\beta - \\alpha + \\phi)\\cos\\phi"
  title=""
/>

Dividing both sides:

<DisplayEquation
  equation="\\tan(\\beta - \\alpha + \\phi)          = \\frac{\\cos\\phi}{\\sin\\phi}           = \\cot\\phi"
  title=""
/>

Using identity:

<DisplayEquation
  equation="\\tan(\\beta - \\alpha + \\phi)    = \\tan(90^\\circ - \\phi)"
  title=""
/>

    <!--FYI equations have to be on one line or else the newline character gets interpreted and everythign breaks - Kevin Wandke-->
Equating arguments:

<DisplayEquation
  equation="\\beta - \\alpha + \\phi = 90^\\circ - \\phi"
  title=""
/>

Solving for phi:

<DisplayEquation
  equation="\\boxed{\\phi = 45^\\circ - \\frac{\\beta}{2} + \\frac{\\alpha}{2}}"
  title=""
/>

This proves:

Increase in rake angle (<InlineEquation equation="\\alpha" />)
and decrease in friction angle (<InlineEquation equation="\\beta" />)

<Itemize>

    <Item>higher shear angle  </Item>
    <Item>lower shear plane area  </Item>
    <Item>less force needed  </Item>
    <Item>lower power and temperature  </Item>

</Itemize>

<DisplayEquation equation="P = u_t MRR = 1.64 \\text{ hp}" title="" />


<DisplayEquation equation="F_c = \\frac{P}{V} = 349 \\text{ lbf}" title="" />


<DisplayEquation equation="t = \\frac{l}{fN} = 0.25 \\text{ min}" title="" />

</SubSubSection>
