<SubSection title="Machining Economics" id="Machining Economics">
<p>*Callout: Maximizing production rate minimizes cutting time per unit.</p>
<p>Terms: total time per unit product for operation <InlineEquation equation="t_c" />, part handling time per part <InlineEquation equation="t_h" />, machining time per part <InlineEquation equation="t_m" />, tool change time <InlineEquation equation="t_t" />, number of pieces cut in one tool life <InlineEquation equation="n_p" /></p>
<Itemize>

    <Item>Total cycle time: <InlineEquation equation="t_c = t_h + t_m + \\frac{t_t}{n_p}" /></Item>

</Itemize>
<p>Terms: cost rate for operator and machine <InlineEquation equation="C_o" />, cost of part handling time <InlineEquation equation="C_o t_h" />, cost of tool change time <InlineEquation equation="\\frac{C_o t_t}{n_p}" />, cost per cutting edge <InlineEquation equation="C_t" />, tooling cost <InlineEquation equation="\\frac{C_t}{n_p}" /></p>
<Itemize>

    <Item>Total cost per unit product for operation: <InlineEquation equation="C_c = C_o t_h + C_o t_m + \\frac{C_o t_t}{n_p} + \\frac{C_t}{n_p}" /></Item>

</Itemize>
</SubSection>
